        "comment": "expanded from The Numbers, Kodak, Box Office Mojo, Variety, the Hollywood Reporter, and the Guardian",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=The Numbers; Kodak; Box Office Mojo; Variety, 20 April 2025; Hollywood Reporter, 21 April 2025; Guardian, 19 April 2025}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Sinners (2025 film)\n| writer = Ryan Coogler\n| director = Ryan Coogler\n| company = Warner Bros.\n| released = 18 April 2025, wide and IMAX, United States\n| rating = R\n| runtime = 137 minutes\n| budget = $90,000,000\n| opening = $48,007,468\n| theaters = 3,308 North American, opening weekend\n| domestic = $279,989,632\n| international = $91,579,127\n| worldwide = $371,568,759\n| working title = Grilled Cheese\n| rights = revert to Ryan Coogler in 25 years\n| cinematographer = Autumn Durald Arkapaw\n| negative = 5-perf 65mm and 15-perf IMAX\n| stocks = Kodak Vision3 500T 5219 and 65mm Ektachrome 100D 5294\n| shoot = 66 days, April to July 2024, southeastern Louisiana\n}}\n\n'''Sinners''' is a film written and directed by Ryan Coogler. Warner Bros. gave it a wide and IMAX release in the United States on 18 April 2025. The Numbers lists the rating as R, the running time as 137 minutes, and the production budget as $90,000,000.<ref name=\"numbers\">The Numbers, title page for Sinners (2025). https://www.the-numbers.com/movie/Sinners-(2025)</ref> Kodak's account of the shoot gives the working title as Grilled Cheese.<ref name=\"kodak\">Kodak, motion-picture account of the Sinners production. https://www.kodak.com/en/motion/blog-post/sinners/</ref> The Hollywood Reporter, on 21 April 2025, reported that the rights revert back to Coogler in 25 years.<ref name=\"thr\">Hollywood Reporter, 21 April 2025. https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/sinners-box-office-minecraft-1236196026/</ref>\n\n== What the brothers do ==\nThe Numbers synopsis is one sentence. Twin brothers return to their hometown to start again, only to discover that an even greater evil is waiting to welcome them back.<ref name=\"numbers\" /> Kodak names them. Smoke and Stack are identical twins and WWI veterans, both played by Michael B. Jordan. They return to Clarksdale, Mississippi, buy a sawmill, and open a juke joint besieged by supernatural forces and the undead.<ref name=\"kodak\" /> The Numbers sentence stops at the evil waiting. The Kodak sentence names the town, the building they buy, the room they open, and what besieges it.<ref name=\"numbers\" /><ref name=\"kodak\" />\n\nHailee Steinfeld plays Mary. Jack O'Connell plays Remmick. Wunmi Mosaku plays Annie. Miles Canton plays Sammie Moore. Kodak also names Delroy Lindo.<ref name=\"kodak\" /> The Numbers page does not carry the cast list. The Kodak page does not carry the budget.<ref name=\"numbers\" /><ref name=\"kodak\" />\n\n== The negative ==\nKodak says the film was shot on 5-perf 65mm and 15-perf IMAX, mainly on Kodak Vision3 500T 5219, plus 65mm Ektachrome 100D 5294 manufactured by Kodak specially for the production.<ref name=\"kodak\" /> The same page says Autumn Durald Arkapaw is \"the first female DP to shoot 65mm in IMAX format\" and the first to combine Ultra Panavision 70 (2.76:1) and IMAX (1.43:1) in one production.<ref name=\"kodak\" /> The shoot was 66 days, April through July 2024, in southeastern Louisiana. The working title during that shoot was Grilled Cheese.<ref name=\"kodak\" /> The Guardian's review, dated 19 April 2025, says the film was shot on 70mm.<ref name=\"guardian\">Guardian review, 19 April 2025. https://www.theguardian.com/film/2025/apr/19/sinners-review-ryan-coogler-sexy-southern-gothic-horror-michael-b-jordan</ref> The review date is the day after the release date on The Numbers.<ref name=\"guardian\" /><ref name=\"numbers\" />\n\n== Opening weekend ==\nVariety, on 20 April 2025, reported an opening weekend of $48 million from 3,308 North American theaters. The same story says Warner spent $90 million.<ref name=\"variety\">Variety, 20 April 2025. https://variety.com/2025/film/box-office/sinners-box-office-opening-weekend-strong-michael-b-jordan-ryan-coogler-1236373417/</ref> Box Office Mojo lists the opening at $48,007,468.<ref name=\"mojo\">Box Office Mojo, Sinners (2025). https://www.boxofficemojo.com/title/tt31193180/</ref> Variety's figure is the weekend rounded in the trade. Mojo's figure is the opening on the gross page. The theater count is Variety's.<ref name=\"variety\" /><ref name=\"mojo\" /> The Numbers budget is a field on a title page. Variety's spend is a sentence in an opening-weekend story dated 20 April 2025, two days after the release.<ref name=\"numbers\" /><ref name=\"variety\" />\n\n== The gross ==\nBox Office Mojo lists domestic receipts of $279,989,632, international receipts of $91,579,127, and a worldwide total of $371,568,759.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> The domestic figure and the international figure are the two components Mojo adds toward that worldwide total. The opening is listed separately from the domestic cumulative.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> The Reporter's 21 April 2025 story is the rights story, the day after Variety's opening report. That sentence is not a gross. The grosses live on the Mojo page. The 25 years live in the Reporter.<ref name=\"mojo\" /><ref name=\"thr\" />\n\nThe working title was Grilled Cheese. The rights go back to Coogler in 25 years. The budget was $90 million.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Films]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
