        "comment": "expanded from Fortune, CNN, ABC, the team page, the Academy board list, and WDSU",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Fortune, 23 September 2025; CNN, 18 September 2025; ABC, 18 September 2025; Turning Point USA team page; U.S. Air Force Academy Board of Visitors; WDSU, 10 March 2026}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Erika Kirk\n| birth name = Erika Lane Frantzve\n| born = 20 November 1988\n| education = political science, Arizona State University\n| pageant = Miss Arizona USA, 2012, as CNN reported it\n| at 18 = founded Everyday Heroes Like You\n| 2016 = created BIBLEin365\n| 2018 = launched Proclaim Streetwear\n| program = hosts Midweek Rise Up\n| elected = CEO and chair, Turning Point USA, unanimous board vote\n| age then = 36\n| staff = 450, as Fortune cites the organization website\n| campuses = 3,500, as Fortune cites the organization website\n| team page = CEO and Chair\n| academy board = Board of Visitors, U.S. Air Force Academy\n}}\n\n'''Erika Kirk''' was born Erika Lane Frantzve on 20 November 1988.<ref name=\"fortune\">Fortune, 23 September 2025. https://fortune.com/2025/09/23/erika-kirk-ceo-turning-point-charlie-speech-children-clothing-brand-career/</ref> CNN, writing on 18 September 2025, gives the birth name as Erika Frantzve, without the middle name, and says she studied political science at Arizona State University and won Miss Arizona USA in 2012.<ref name=\"cnn\">CNN, 18 September 2025. https://www.cnn.com/2025/09/18/politics/erika-kirk-turning-point-ceo</ref> Fortune's name has three parts. CNN's name, in that story, has two. The birth date is Fortune's. The pageant year and the university are CNN's.<ref name=\"fortune\" /><ref name=\"cnn\" />\n\n== The things she started ==\nFortune says that at 18 she founded Everyday Heroes Like You, that in 2016 she created BIBLEin365, and that in 2018 she launched Proclaim Streetwear. She hosts Midweek Rise Up.<ref name=\"fortune\" /> The Proclaim line, as Fortune prints it, is: \"At PROCLAIM, we believe that honoring God means honoring the work of honest hands.\"<ref name=\"fortune\" /> Fortune dates the streetwear launch to 2018 and prints the line from the brand.<ref name=\"fortune\" />\n\n== The vote ==\nEight days after Charlie Kirk was shot and killed, the Turning Point USA board unanimously elected her, then 36, CEO and chair.<ref name=\"fortune\" /> ABC, on 18 September 2025, reported that the board unanimously elected her CEO and chair.<ref name=\"abc\">ABC News, 18 September 2025. https://abcnews.com/US/erika-kirk-elected-new-ceo-turning-point-usa/story?id=125707736</ref> The team page lists her as CEO and Chair.<ref name=\"team\">Turning Point USA, team page. https://tpusa.com/team/</ref> Fortune says the organization has 450 staff and a presence on 3,500 campuses, according to its website.<ref name=\"fortune\" /> The staff count and the campus count are figures the organization states on its own site, carried in Fortune. ABC's report and Fortune's report agree on the offices. Fortune is the one that adds the eight days and the age.<ref name=\"fortune\" /><ref name=\"abc\" /><ref name=\"team\" />\n\n== 18 September and 23 September ==\nCNN's 18 September 2025 story is the same calendar day as ABC's election story. Miss Arizona USA 2012 is printed in the CNN story as a thing she won. The CNN story does not attach a class year to the political science study.<ref name=\"cnn\" /> ABC, on that day, has the election and not the pageant.<ref name=\"abc\" /> Fortune, five days later, gives Erika Lane Frantzve and the date of birth.<ref name=\"fortune\" />\n\n== The academy seat ==\nThe U.S. Air Force Academy Board of Visitors lists Erika Kirk among the members Appointed by the President. The page does not give the date of the appointment.<ref name=\"bov\">U.S. Air Force Academy, Board of Visitors. https://www.usafa.edu/about/bov/</ref> WDSU, on 10 March 2026, reported that President Trump appointed her to that board, replacing her husband, on a board of 16 members.<ref name=\"wdsu\">WDSU, 10 March 2026. https://www.wdsu.com/article/erika-kirk-appointed-air-force-academy-board/70699762</ref> The academy page shows her on the list. The WDSU story names the president who appointed her, the person she replaced, and the size of the board.<ref name=\"bov\" /><ref name=\"wdsu\" />\n\nThe streetwear line was already called Proclaim. Eight days later the board made her chair. In March 2026 the academy board seat changed names.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:People]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
