        "comment": "expanded from Billboard, CBS, CNN, the Guardian, Deadline, and WWE",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Billboard artist page; CBS, 9 February 2026; CNN fast facts, updated 8 September 2026; Guardian, 1 February 2026; Deadline, 29 September 2025; WWE, 10 April 2021}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Bad Bunny\n| name = Benito Antonio Martínez Ocasio\n| born = 10 March 1994\n| birthplace = Bayamón, Puerto Rico\n| raised = Puerto Rico\n| hot 100 = I Like It, No. 1, July 2018\n| spanish album = El Último Tour del Mundo, first all-Spanish No. 1 on the Billboard 200\n| verano = Un Verano Sin Ti, 13 weeks at No. 1, top Billboard 200 album of 2022\n| fotos = Debí Tirar Más Fotos, fourth Billboard 200 No. 1\n| grammy = Album of the Year, Debí Tirar Más Fotos\n| halftime = 8 February 2026, Santa Clara\n| spotify morning = top 6, U.S. Top 50, led by DtMF\n| streamed = Spotify most-streamed artist of 2025\n| wrestlemania = WrestleMania 37, with Damian Priest\n}}\n\n'''Bad Bunny''' is Benito Antonio Martínez Ocasio. CNN's fast facts, updated 8 September 2026, give the birth date as 10 March 1994 and the birthplace as Bayamón, Puerto Rico, and give the birth name in full.<ref name=\"cnn\">CNN fast facts, updated 8 September 2026. https://www.cnn.com/us/bad-bunny-fast-facts</ref> Billboard gives the name as Benito Martínez Ocasio, the birthday as 10 March 1994, and the place as born and raised in Puerto Rico.<ref name=\"billboard\">Billboard, artist page for Bad Bunny. https://www.billboard.com/artist/bad-bunny/</ref> CBS, on 9 February 2026, uses the full name Benito Antonio Martínez Ocasio.<ref name=\"cbs\">CBS News, 9 February 2026. https://www.cbsnews.com/news/bad-bunny-spotify-super-bowl-halftime-performance/</ref> The middle name Antonio is on CNN and CBS. Billboard's page, as cited here, prints Benito Martínez Ocasio.<ref name=\"cnn\" /><ref name=\"cbs\" /><ref name=\"billboard\" />\n\n== The charts ==\n\"I Like It,\" with Cardi B and J Balvin, reached No. 1 on the Hot 100 in July 2018.<ref name=\"billboard\" /> ''El Último Tour del Mundo'' was the first all-Spanish language album to hit No. 1 on the Billboard 200.<ref name=\"billboard\" /> ''Un Verano Sin Ti'' spent 13 weeks at No. 1 and was the top Billboard 200 album of 2022.<ref name=\"billboard\" /> ''Debí Tirar Más Fotos'' is, on the Billboard page, his fourth Billboard 200 No. 1. The same page says he later won Album of the Year for it, and that the album was the backdrop of an all-Spanish Super Bowl halftime show in 2026.<ref name=\"billboard\" /> The Guardian, on 1 February 2026, lists the Album of the Year Grammy with ''Debí Tirar Más Fotos'' as the winner.<ref name=\"guardian\">Guardian, 1 February 2026, Grammy winners. https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/feb/01/grammy-awards-2026-winners</ref>\n\n== Santa Clara ==\nCBS reported that he headlined the Super Bowl halftime show on 8 February 2026 in Santa Clara, that the performance was the first sung primarily in Spanish, and that early figures put the audience above 135 million, the most-watched Super Bowl halftime performance of all time.<ref name=\"cbs\" /> Billboard's wording for the language of that show is \"all-Spanish.\" CBS's wording is \"primarily in Spanish.\" They are not the same adverb.<ref name=\"billboard\" /><ref name=\"cbs\" /> The morning after, CBS wrote, he held the top 6 spots on Spotify's U.S. Top 50, led by DtMF. CBS also calls him Spotify's most-streamed artist of 2025.<ref name=\"cbs\" /> The morning is 9 February 2026, the date of the CBS story, about a show dated the day before. The six spots are a U.S. Spotify chart, not the Billboard 200.<ref name=\"cbs\" />\n\n== September, before the show ==\nOn 29 September 2025, in an Apple Music interview reported by Deadline, he said: \"I'm really excited for my friends, my family. Puerto Rico, all the Latino people around the world. I'm excited about my culture. I'm excited about everything, not just for me.\"<ref name=\"deadline\">Deadline, 29 September 2025. https://deadline.com/2025/09/bad-bunny-super-bowl-lx-performance-puerto-rico-jay-z-halftime-show-1236565333/</ref> The interview date is before the Santa Clara show and before the Guardian's Grammy list. The sentence names friends, family, Puerto Rico, and Latino people around the world. It does not name a chart position.<ref name=\"deadline\" />\n\n== The tag match ==\nWWE published the result on 10 April 2021 and called the match his first. At WrestleMania 37 he and Damian Priest defeated The Miz and John Morrison. WWE calls it his first-ever WWE match.<ref name=\"wwe\">WWE, WrestleMania 37 results, published 10 April 2021. https://www.wwe.com/shows/wrestlemania/wrestlemania-37/bad-bunny-damian-priest-vs-the-miz-john-morrison-results</ref>\n\nThe next morning he held the top six on the American Spotify chart. The show the night before was in Spanish. In 2021 he won a tag match at WrestleMania.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Music]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
