        "daysAgo": 4,
        "comment": "expanded from the BBC, Sony, the Los Angeles Times, Den of Geek, Deadline, and two Guardian pieces",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=BBC, 23 June 2015; Sony Pictures, 23 June 2015; Los Angeles Times, 14 June 2023; Den of Geek; Deadline, 16 December 2021; Guardian, 24 January 2022; Guardian, 6 February 2024}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Tom Holland\n| full name = Thomas Stanley Holland\n| born = Kingston-upon-Thames, London, 1996\n| stage role = Billy in Billy Elliot the Musical\n| also = Michael, Billy's friend, then the lead\n| auditions = eight, in the BBC account\n| training = two years\n| stage debut = 2008\n| caster = Stephen Daldry\n| reason = he reminded Daldry of Jamie Bell\n| marvel = Peter Parker, announced 23 June 2015\n| director = Jon Watts\n| spider-man release = 28 July 2017\n| nose = last day of The Lost City of Z, Colombia\n| told marvel = he fell over\n| boots = a backflip in leather boots\n| lip sync = Rihanna, Umbrella, 2017\n| uncharted = young Nathan Drake, United States release 18 February\n| romeo = Duke of York's, from 11 May, 12 weeks\n}}\n\n'''Thomas Stanley Holland''' was born in Kingston-upon-Thames, London, in 1996.<ref name=\"bbc\">BBC News, 23 June 2015. https://www.bbc.com/news/newsbeat-33248311</ref> The stage part was Billy in ''Billy Elliot the Musical''.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> Stephen Daldry cast him.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The reason was that Holland reminded Daldry of Jamie Bell.<ref name=\"bbc\" />\n\n== Eight auditions, and Michael ==\nThe BBC, on 23 June 2015, said the role followed eight auditions.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The training lasted two years.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The stage debut was in 2008.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The Guardian, on 24 January 2022, describes the same years from the other end of the billing.<ref name=\"g22\">The Guardian, 24 January 2022. https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/jan/24/tom-holland-actor-billy-elliot-to-spider-man</ref> After two years of preparation he was on stage first as Michael.<ref name=\"g22\" /> Michael is Billy's friend.<ref name=\"g22\" /> He then played Billy.<ref name=\"g22\" /> That Guardian piece places the double step in 2008.<ref name=\"g22\" /> A later Guardian piece is dated 6 February 2024.<ref name=\"g24\">The Guardian, 6 February 2024. https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2024/feb/06/tom-holland-spider-man-shakespeare-romeo-west-end-jamie-lloyd</ref> It gives the same order of parts.<ref name=\"g24\" /> The 2024 piece says he joined in the supporting part.<ref name=\"g24\" /> The part it names first is the supporting role of Billy's friend Michael.<ref name=\"g24\" /> The lead came after that.<ref name=\"g24\" /> The eight auditions are the BBC's sentence.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The first billing as Michael is the Guardian's sentence.<ref name=\"g22\" />\n\n== Peter Parker ==\nSony and Marvel announced the next part on 23 June 2015.<ref name=\"sony\">Sony Pictures, 23 June 2015. https://www.sonypictures.com/corp/press_releases/2015/06_15/062315_hollandspiderman.html</ref> He would play Peter Parker.<ref name=\"sony\" /> The director named was Jon Watts.<ref name=\"sony\" /> The release date named was 28 July 2017.<ref name=\"sony\" /> Amy Pascal said, \"With Tom, we've found the perfect actor to bring Spider-Man's story into the Marvel Cinematic Universe.\"<ref name=\"sony\" /> The January 2022 Guardian said ''Spider-Man: No Way Home'' had grossed more than $1.6 billion.<ref name=\"g22\" />\n\n== The boots ==\nAt the New York Film Festival in 2016, via Den of Geek, he described the last day of ''The Lost City of Z''.<ref name=\"dog\">Den of Geek. https://www.denofgeek.com/culture/tom-holland-talks-breaking-his-nose-on-the-lost-city-of-z/</ref> The shoot was in Colombia.<ref name=\"dog\" /> He broke his nose.<ref name=\"dog\" /> He said, \"I had these stupid leather boots on, I tried to do a backflip, and just broke my face.\"<ref name=\"dog\" /> He told Marvel, \"Oh, I just fell over.\"<ref name=\"dog\" /> The rest of that account was, \"Bashed it out.\"<ref name=\"dog\" />\n\n== Fishnets ==\nThe Los Angeles Times, on 14 June 2023, returned to a 2017 ''Lip Sync Battle''.<ref name=\"lat\">Los Angeles Times, 14 June 2023. https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/music/story/2023-06-14/tom-holland-interview-lip-sync-battle-rihanna</ref> The song was Rihanna's \"Umbrella.\"<ref name=\"lat\" /> He began in a fedora and a suit.<ref name=\"lat\" /> The costume then became latex shorts, a halter, and fishnets.<ref name=\"lat\" /> Zendaya did Bruno Mars's \"24K Magic.\"<ref name=\"lat\" /> He told The Hollywood Reporter, via the Los Angeles Times, \"I'm proud of it.\"<ref name=\"lat\" /> Asked if the number was meant to defy toxic masculinity, he said, \"No.\"<ref name=\"lat\" /> He added, \"Mm-mm.\"<ref name=\"lat\" /> He said, \"Yeah, I'll put some fishnets on and dance in the rain.\"<ref name=\"lat\" />\n\n== Drake, then the Duke of York's ==\n''Uncharted'' casts him as young Nathan Drake.<ref name=\"dl\">Deadline, 16 December 2021. https://deadline.com/2021/12/uncharted-sony-unveils-first-poster-for-tom-holland-pic-1234892731/</ref> Mark Wahlberg plays Victor Sully Sullivan.<ref name=\"dl\" /> Ruben Fleischer directed.<ref name=\"dl\" /> The film is based on the Naughty Dog games.<ref name=\"dl\" /> Deadline, on 16 December 2021, gives a United States release of 18 February.<ref name=\"dl\" /> The February 2024 Guardian places ''Romeo and Juliet'' at the Duke of York's.<ref name=\"g24\" /> The run starts on 11 May.<ref name=\"g24\" /> The booking is 12 weeks.<ref name=\"g24\" />\n\nHe told Marvel he fell over. He had tried a backflip in leather boots.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Actors]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
