        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Box Office Mojo; The Numbers; Variety, 22 August 2025; Deadline, 20 November 2025; Rolling Stone, 10 August 2025; IndieWire, 6 November 2025; /Film, 8 August 2025}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Weapons (2025 film)\n| writer = Zach Cregger\n| director = Zach Cregger\n| companies = New Line, Warner Bros.\n| domestic release = 8 August 2025\n| earliest listed date = 6 August 2025\n| rating = R\n| runtime = 2 hours 8 minutes\n| opening = $43,501,217\n| domestic = $151,572,492\n| international = $118,500,000\n| worldwide = $270,072,492\n| variety opening = $42.5 million on 22 August 2025\n| variety two-week domestic = $100.3 million\n| variety international then = $72.3 million\n| variety worldwide then = $172.6 million\n| variety production cost = $38 million\n| deadline net budget = $38 million\n| deadline gross = over $268 million\n| indiewire worldwide = $267 million on 6 November 2025\n| rolling stone deal = $38 million for the script\n| departure = 2:17 a.m.\n| song = George Harrison, Beware of Darkness\n| gladys = Amy Madigan\n}}\n\n'''Weapons''' is a film written and directed by Zach Cregger.<ref name=\"var\">Variety, 22 August 2025. https://variety.com/2025/film/news/weapons-box-office-100-million-zach-cregger-1236495987/</ref> New Line is the banner in Variety's account.<ref name=\"var\" /> Warner Bros. is the domestic distributor.<ref name=\"mojo\">Box Office Mojo. https://www.boxofficemojo.com/title/tt26581740/</ref> The domestic release date is 8 August 2025.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> The Numbers lists that date as well.<ref name=\"num\">The Numbers. https://www.the-numbers.com/movie/Weapons-(2025)</ref> The earliest listed date is 6 August 2025.<ref name=\"mojo\" />\n\n== The same night ==\nBox Office Mojo's logline says all but one child from the same class vanish.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> They vanish on the same night.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> They vanish at exactly the same time.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> Variety describes 17 school children from the same class.<ref name=\"var\" /> They are missing in the middle of the night.<ref name=\"var\" /> The clock time in that story is 2:17 a.m.<ref name=\"var\" /> /Film, on 8 August 2025, also puts the departure at that hour.<ref name=\"slash\">/Film, 8 August 2025. https://www.slashfilm.com/1921716/weapons-director-zach-cregger-horror-movie-inspirations-exclusive-interview/</ref> The rating on the Mojo page is R.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> The running time is 2 hours 8 minutes.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> The Numbers agrees on the rating.<ref name=\"num\" /> It agrees on the running time.<ref name=\"num\" />\n\n== Dated grosses ==\nVariety's box-office story is dated 22 August 2025.<ref name=\"var\" /> The opening in that story is $42.5 million.<ref name=\"var\" /> Domestic receipts after two weeks were $100.3 million.<ref name=\"var\" /> International receipts then were $72.3 million.<ref name=\"var\" /> The worldwide total then was $172.6 million.<ref name=\"var\" /> IndieWire's interview is dated 6 November 2025.<ref name=\"iw\">IndieWire, 6 November 2025. https://www.indiewire.com/features/interviews/weapons-ending-zach-cregger-interview-amy-madigan-1235159153/</ref> The worldwide figure there is $267 million.<ref name=\"iw\" /> Deadline's interview is dated 20 November 2025.<ref name=\"dl\">Deadline, 20 November 2025. https://deadline.com/2025/11/zach-cregger-weapons-gladys-movie-resident-evil-interview-1236625248/</ref> The gross in that interview is over $268 million.<ref name=\"dl\" /> Box Office Mojo lists an opening of $43,501,217.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> The domestic total on that page is $151,572,492.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> The international total on that page is $118,500,000.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> The worldwide total on that page is $270,072,492.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> The Numbers prints those four lines as well.<ref name=\"num\" /> Each total stays with the date of the page that printed it.<ref name=\"var\" /><ref name=\"iw\" /><ref name=\"dl\" /><ref name=\"mojo\" />\n\n== Three ways of saying the cost ==\nThe production cost in the Variety story is $38 million.<ref name=\"var\" /> Rolling Stone, on 10 August 2025, described a deal for the script.<ref name=\"rs\">Rolling Stone, 10 August 2025. https://www.rollingstone.com/tv-movies/tv-movie-features/weapons-zach-cregger-interview-1235398084/</ref> The deal was $38 million.<ref name=\"rs\" /> Deadline calls its figure a net budget.<ref name=\"dl\" /> That net budget is $38 million.<ref name=\"dl\" /> His debut was the 2022 film ''Barbarian''.<ref name=\"var\" /> Variety's worldwide gross for that film is $45.4 million.<ref name=\"var\" /> The cost Variety names for it is $4.5 million.<ref name=\"var\" />\n\n== The garage ==\nHe wrote ''Weapons'' in his garage.<ref name=\"dl\" /> A washer stood next to the desk.<ref name=\"dl\" /> A dryer stood there too.<ref name=\"dl\" /> The machines were noisy.<ref name=\"dl\" /> He co-composed the score.<ref name=\"dl\" /> The children run at night.<ref name=\"dl\" /> The song under that running is George Harrison's \"Beware of Darkness.\"<ref name=\"dl\" /> Amy Madigan plays Gladys.<ref name=\"dl\" /> Deadline calls Gladys a twisted witchy aunt.<ref name=\"dl\" /> She has a lock on an entire small town's young children.<ref name=\"dl\" /> The Deadline piece pictures Julia Garner with Cregger.<ref name=\"dl\" />\n\n== What he called the script ==\nHe told Deadline, \"Weapons is autobiographical in a lot of ways.\"<ref name=\"dl\" /> On the Alex chapter he said, \"Anyone who grew up in a household of addiction can smell what's going on in that chapter.\"<ref name=\"dl\" /> He told Rolling Stone, \"Weapons was like me vomiting.\"<ref name=\"rs\" /> Rolling Stone also says 17 children disappear.<ref name=\"rs\" /> He told IndieWire, \"It's a really personal movie for me.\"<ref name=\"iw\" /> He told /Film, \"Weapons is a movie that's very much like me looking inwards.\"<ref name=\"slash\" /> The next sentence of that remark was, \"It's an autobiographical movie in a lot of ways.\"<ref name=\"slash\" />\n\nHe wrote it in a garage next to a washer and a dryer. The children leave at 2:17 a.m. The song under the running is George Harrison.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Films]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
