        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Biography.com, updated 6 January 2026; Deadline, 23 February 2025; Variety, 18 February 2024; Oscars.org, 97th ceremony; Searchlight; Netflix Tudum, 31 January 2025; Academy 90th fact sheet}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Timothée Chalamet\n| born = 27 December 1995, New York City\n| nationality = French-American\n| elio = Call Me by Your Name, 2017\n| first nomination = Actor, 90th Academy Awards\n| paul = Dune, 2021, and Dune: Part Two, 2024\n| wonka = Willy Wonka, 2023\n| wonka gross = $604.9 million worldwide after 10 weeks\n| dylan = Bob Dylan in A Complete Unknown, 2024\n| sag = 23 February 2025, lead actor, Dylan\n| oscars 97 = nominee, Actor in a Leading Role\n| oscar winner = Adrien Brody, The Brutalist\n| film nominations = 8, for A Complete Unknown\n| dune part two camera = Greig Fraser\n}}\n\n'''Timothée Chalamet''' was born on 27 December 1995.<ref name=\"bio\">Biography.com, updated 6 January 2026. https://www.biography.com/actors/timothee-chalamet</ref> The city was New York City.<ref name=\"bio\" /> He is French-American.<ref name=\"bio\" /> Biography.com's page carries an update date of 6 January 2026.<ref name=\"bio\" />\n\n== Elio ==\nThe breakout part was Elio Perlman.<ref name=\"bio\" /> The film was ''Call Me by Your Name''.<ref name=\"bio\" /> The year was 2017.<ref name=\"bio\" /> The nomination was for Best Actor.<ref name=\"bio\" /> It was his first Oscar nomination.<ref name=\"sheet\">Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences, 90th Academy Awards fact sheet. https://www.oscars.org/sites/oscars/files/90th-factsheet.pdf</ref> The 90th fact sheet names him as Elio in that film.<ref name=\"sheet\" /> The sheet's line is that this is his first nomination.<ref name=\"sheet\" />\n\n== Paul, then Willy ==\nHe plays Paul Atreides in ''Dune''.<ref name=\"tudum\">Netflix Tudum, 31 January 2025. https://www.netflix.com/tudum/articles/dune-part-two-netflix-date-cast-details</ref> The first film's year is 2021.<ref name=\"bio\" /> ''Dune: Part Two'' followed in 2024.<ref name=\"bio\" /> Tudum's piece is dated 31 January 2025.<ref name=\"tudum\" /> The novel under the films is Frank Herbert's.<ref name=\"tudum\" /> Herbert's book is from 1965.<ref name=\"tudum\" /> Willy Wonka is the part in ''Wonka''.<ref name=\"bio\" /> That film is from 2023.<ref name=\"bio\" /> Variety, on 18 February 2024, counted the gross after 10 weeks.<ref name=\"var\">Variety, 18 February 2024. https://variety.com/2024/film/box-office/timothee-chalamet-wonka-box-office-milestone-600-million-globally-1235915495/</ref> The worldwide figure was $604.9 million.<ref name=\"var\" /> North America was $210 million.<ref name=\"var\" /> International receipts were $395.1 million.<ref name=\"var\" />\n\n== Dylan ==\nHe plays Bob Dylan in ''A Complete Unknown''.<ref name=\"bio\" /> The film is from 2024.<ref name=\"bio\" /> The performance brought another Best Actor nomination.<ref name=\"bio\" /> Searchlight says he stars.<ref name=\"search\">Searchlight Pictures. https://www.searchlightpictures.com/a-complete-unknown/</ref> Searchlight says he sings.<ref name=\"search\" /> The part he sings is Bob Dylan.<ref name=\"search\" /> The film's Academy Award nominations number 8.<ref name=\"search\" /> That count belongs to the film.<ref name=\"search\" />\n\n== The guild, then the Oscar ==\nThe Screen Actors Guild award came on 23 February 2025.<ref name=\"dl\">Deadline, 23 February 2025. https://deadline.com/2025/02/timothee-chalamet-sag-awards-speech-actor-1236299554/</ref> The category was Outstanding Performance by a Male Actor in a Leading Role.<ref name=\"dl\" /> The performance was the Dylan one.<ref name=\"dl\" /> He said, \"I want to be one of the greats.\"<ref name=\"dl\" /> Oscars.org's page for the 97th ceremony is dated 2 March 2025.<ref name=\"oscars\">Oscars.org, 97th Academy Awards. https://www.oscars.org/oscars/ceremonies/2025</ref> He was a nominee for Actor in a Leading Role.<ref name=\"oscars\" /> The film on that nomination is ''A Complete Unknown''.<ref name=\"oscars\" /> The winner was Adrien Brody.<ref name=\"oscars\" /> Brody's film was ''The Brutalist''.<ref name=\"oscars\" /> ''Dune: Part Two'' is listed for cinematography.<ref name=\"oscars\" /> The cinematographer is Greig Fraser.<ref name=\"oscars\" /> The film is also among the best picture nominees.<ref name=\"oscars\" /> Mary Parent is one of the named producers.<ref name=\"oscars\" /> Cale Boyter is another.<ref name=\"oscars\" /> Tanya Lapointe is another.<ref name=\"oscars\" /> Denis Villeneuve is another.<ref name=\"oscars\" />\n\nHe said he wanted to be one of the greats. The award in his hand that night was from the Screen Actors Guild, for playing Bob Dylan. The Oscar that year went to Adrien Brody.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Actors]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
