        "content": "{{true and funny|source=BBC, 26 August 2026; ABC, 26 August 2026; Guardian, 26 August 2026; 20th Century Studios; BFI Screenonline; AFI Catalog}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Tim Curry\n| born = Warrington, 1946\n| bfi wording = Cheshire-born\n| frank stage = Royal Court, 1973\n| frank film = The Rocky Horror Picture Show\n| studios date = 23 February 1975\n| afi header = September 1975\n| studios runtime = 1 hour 39 minutes\n| afi runtime = 98 minutes, or 100 to 101 minutes\n| studios rating = R\n| clue = Wadsworth, 1985\n| pennywise = It, 1990 television\n| thornberry = Nigel Thornberry, The Wild Thornberrys\n| emmy = Daytime Emmy, Captain Hook, Peter Pan and the Pirates\n| stroke = 2012\n| died = 25 August 2026, Toluca Lake, Los Angeles\n| age = 80, in the Guardian\n| manager = Marcia Hurwitz\n}}\n\n'''Tim Curry''' was born in Warrington in 1946.<ref name=\"bbc\">BBC News, 26 August 2026. https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5yd92gkk7vo</ref> BFI Screenonline calls him Cheshire-born.<ref name=\"bfi\">BFI Screenonline. http://www.screenonline.org.uk/people/id/861193/</ref> The two place-names are what those sources print.<ref name=\"bbc\" /><ref name=\"bfi\" />\n\n== Frank-N-Furter ==\nHe originated Dr. Frank-N-Furter on stage.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The theatre was the Royal Court.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The year was 1973.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> He played the part again in the 1975 film.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> 20th Century Studios credits Tim Curry as Dr. Frank-N-Furter.<ref name=\"fox\">20th Century Studios. https://www.20thcenturystudios.com/movies/the-rocky-horror-picture-show</ref> The AFI Catalog calls that performance his feature film debut.<ref name=\"afi\">AFI Catalog. https://catalog.afi.com/Film/55624-THE-ROCKYHORRORPICTURESHOW</ref> BFI Screenonline credits ''The Rocky Horror Picture Show'' to Jim Sharman.<ref name=\"bfi\" /> The BFI year is 1975.<ref name=\"bfi\" /> The same BFI page says he played Mozart in ''Amadeus'' on Broadway.<ref name=\"bfi\" />\n\n== February, and September ==\nThe 20th Century Studios page prints a release date of 23 February 1975.<ref name=\"fox\" /> The runtime on that page is 1 hour 39 minutes.<ref name=\"fox\" /> The rating on that page is R.<ref name=\"fox\" /> The AFI Catalog header prints September 1975.<ref name=\"afi\" /> One AFI running time is 98 minutes.<ref name=\"afi\" /> Another printing on that header is 100 to 101 minutes.<ref name=\"afi\" /> The February date is what the studio page prints.<ref name=\"fox\" /> The September header is what the AFI catalog prints.<ref name=\"afi\" />\n\n== The butler ==\nABC's obituary, on 26 August 2026, names the butler Wadsworth in ''Clue''.<ref name=\"abc\">ABC News, 26 August 2026. https://abcnews.com/GMA/Culture/tim-curry-rocky-horror-picture-show-clue-actor/story?id=106455175</ref> The film is from 1985.<ref name=\"abc\" /> He voiced Nigel Thornberry on ''The Wild Thornberrys''.<ref name=\"abc\" /> A Daytime Emmy came for Captain Hook.<ref name=\"abc\" /> The series was ''Peter Pan and the Pirates''.<ref name=\"abc\" /> He played Pennywise in the 1990 television ''It''.<ref name=\"bbc\" />\n\n== 2012 ==\nA major stroke came in 2012.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> He used a wheelchair afterward.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The work that followed was voice acting.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The Guardian, on 26 August 2026, printed his line about the stroke.<ref name=\"gu\">The Guardian, 26 August 2026. https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/aug/26/tim-curry-dies-rocky-horror-show-stephen-king-it-legend-film</ref> He said, \"I knew I had to force myself to relax and just take the opportunity to float a little.\"<ref name=\"gu\" /> The stroke happened during a massage.<ref name=\"gu\" /> He had brain surgery.<ref name=\"gu\" />\n\n== Which obituary holds which credit ==\nThe wheelchair and the later voice work are the BBC's order.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The Guardian's account of the stroke names the massage.<ref name=\"gu\" /> The same account names the surgery.<ref name=\"gu\" /> It also prints his sentence about floating.<ref name=\"gu\" /> ABC is the obituary that lists Wadsworth.<ref name=\"abc\" /> The same obituary lists Nigel Thornberry.<ref name=\"abc\" /> The Daytime Emmy in that obituary is for Captain Hook.<ref name=\"abc\" /> ''Peter Pan and the Pirates'' is the series on that Emmy.<ref name=\"abc\" /> Pennywise is the part in the television ''It''.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The BBC dates that television part separately from the film catalogs.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The studio page and the AFI header remain two release lines.<ref name=\"fox\" /><ref name=\"afi\" />\n\n== Toluca Lake ==\nHis manager, Marcia Hurwitz, said he passed away peacefully.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The place was his home in Toluca Lake.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The city was Los Angeles.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The day was 25 August.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The BBC reported her statement on 26 August 2026.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The Guardian reported that he died at 80.<ref name=\"gu\" />\n\nIn Clue he is the butler in every ending. He died at home in Toluca Lake on 25 August 2026. After 2012 the work was voice.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Actors]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
