        "comment": "expanded from the UN proclamation, the UN member-state note, the UK toponymic factfile, the Guardian, MDPI, and caboverde-info",
        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Statement by President Aristides Pereira to the United Nations; UN member-state note, 24 October 2013; UK Cape Verde toponymic factfile; Guardian, 17 December 2011; peer-reviewed paper on surface water; caboverde-info, Streams}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Cape Verde\n| proclaimed = 5 July 1975\n| proclamation by = President Aristides Pereira\n| un name change = 24 October 2013, from The Republic of Cape Verde\n| how = a request to the Secretary-General\n| islands = 10\n| inhabited = 9\n| islets = 8\n| capital = Praia\n| official language = Portuguese\n| national language = Cape Verdean Creole\n| creole = mother tongue of almost all Cape Verdeans\n| evora born = 27 August 1941, Mindelo, São Vicente\n| evora died = 17 December 2011, aged 70\n| sang = morna, barefoot\n| fresh water = no permanent surface stock\n| streams = ribeiras, almost always dry\n}}\n\n'''Cape Verde''' is the republic President Aristides Pereira told the United Nations \"was proclaimed on 5 July 1975.\"<ref name=\"treaty\">Statement of President Aristides Pereira, deposited with the United Nations. https://treaties.un.org/doc/source/docs/caboverde.pdf</ref> On 24 October 2013 the official name was changed from The Republic of Cape Verde, by a request to the Secretary-General.<ref name=\"un\">United Nations, member states. https://www.un.org/en/about-us/member-states/cabo-verde</ref> The country has no permanent surface stock of fresh water.<ref name=\"mdpi\">Peer-reviewed paper. https://www.mdpi.com/2073-445X/4/1/22</ref>\n\n== The proclamation ==\nThe speaker is the president. The document is the one deposited with the treaty records of the United Nations. The name in his sentence is the Republic of Cape Verde.<ref name=\"treaty\" />\n\n== The name at the UN ==\nThe United Nations records the change of official name. The change was made by a request to the Secretary-General.<ref name=\"un\" /> The proclamation and the name change are two different acts. One is Pereira's statement. The other is a request to the Secretary-General.<ref name=\"treaty\" /><ref name=\"un\" /> The proclamation document still uses the Republic of Cape Verde for the day he named.<ref name=\"treaty\" />\n\n== Ten islands ==\nA United Kingdom toponymic factfile counts ten islands, nine of them inhabited, plus eight islets. The capital is Praia.<ref name=\"factfile\">United Kingdom toponymic factfile, Cape Verde. https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/654cfedf014cc90010677386/Cape_Verde_Toponymic_Factfile.pdf</ref> The factfile splits language in one pair of statements. Portuguese is the only official language. Cape Verdean Creole is a recognised national language and the mother tongue of almost all Cape Verdeans.<ref name=\"factfile\" /> \"Only\" applies to the official language. \"Almost all\" applies to the mother tongue. The islets are additional to the islands.<ref name=\"factfile\" />\n\n== Mindelo ==\nCesária Évora was born on 27 August 1941 in Mindelo, on São Vicente. She sang morna. She performed barefoot. She died on 17 December 2011, aged 70.<ref name=\"guardian\">Guardian obituary, 17 December 2011. https://www.theguardian.com/music/2011/dec/17/cesaria-evora</ref> Mindelo, in that obituary, is on São Vicente.<ref name=\"guardian\" />\n\n== No permanent stock ==\nA peer-reviewed paper states the hydrology in one sentence: \"Cape Verde has no permanent surface stock of fresh water.\"<ref name=\"mdpi\" /> A geographical note on the streams says the ribeiras are not fed by perennial sources and are \"almost always dry.\"<ref name=\"streams\">caboverde-info, \"Streams\". https://www.caboverde-info.com/eng/Identity/Geography/Geography-articles/Streams</ref> The paper's phrase is \"permanent surface stock,\" and the stock is fresh water, and the claim is that there is none.<ref name=\"mdpi\" /> The streams page says: \"Ribeiras\" (streams) run through all the islands, however none of these are fed by perennial sources.<ref name=\"streams\" /> The Guardian says: \"She was born in Mindelo, a port city on the island of São Vicente.\"<ref name=\"guardian\" />\n\nThe UN changed the name in 2013. The country still has no permanent surface stock of fresh water, and the ribeiras are almost always dry. She sang barefoot.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Countries]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
