        "content": "{{true and funny|source=The Hindu, 15 March 2026; The Hindu, updated 6 May 2026; BBC, 8 May 2026; Indian Express, updated 5 May 2026; ThePrint, 7 May 2026; Deccan Herald, 5 May 2026}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = 2026 West Bengal Legislative Assembly election\n| polling = 23 April 2026 and 29 April 2026\n| counting = 4 May 2026\n| assembly size = 294 members\n| seats with a count = 293\n| why one seat had no count = countermanded\n| bjp seats in the papers = 207\n| tmc seats = 80\n| tmc in 2021 = 215\n| bjp vote share = 45.84 percent\n| other seats = Congress 2, Aam Janata Unnayan Party 2, CPI(M) 1, AISF 1\n| rolls = about 91 lakh names removed\n| chief minister = Suvendu Adhikari\n| bhabanipur = Adhikari defeated Mamata Banerjee by over 15,000 votes\n| falta = no counting, repoll ordered\n| eci results page = 404 in October 2026\n}}\n\n'''The 2026 West Bengal Legislative Assembly election''' was polled on 23 April 2026 and 29 April 2026.<ref name=\"sched\">The Hindu, 15 March 2026. https://www.thehindu.com/elections/west-bengal-assembly/2026-assembly-elections-schedule-dates-west-bengal-full-schedule/article70746039.ece</ref> Counting was set for 4 May.<ref name=\"sched\" /> The schedule is the 15 March Hindu story.<ref name=\"sched\" />\n\n== 207, and the seat that was not counted ==\nThe Hindu, updated 6 May 2026, said that as of 5 May the Bharatiya Janata Party had 207 of 293 declared seats.<ref name=\"hdata\">The Hindu, updated 6 May 2026. https://www.thehindu.com/data/west-bengal-assembly-elections-results-2026-tmc-bjp-rural-urban-mamata-banerjee/article70938097.ece</ref> Trinamool Congress had 80 on that page.<ref name=\"hdata\" /> The BJP vote share on that page was 45.84 percent.<ref name=\"hdata\" />\n\nThe Indian Express, updated 5 May 2026, also printed 207 out of 293.<ref name=\"ie\">Indian Express, updated 5 May 2026. https://indianexpress.com/article/india/west-bengal-assembly-election-results-2026-winners-constituency-wise-seat-wise-full-list-10665665/</ref> ThePrint, on 7 May 2026, printed 207 of 293 as well.<ref name=\"print\">ThePrint, 7 May 2026. https://theprint.in/politics/did-sir-help-bjp-what-data-reveals-about-fiercely-contested-west-bengal-election/2924217/</ref> The BBC, on 8 May 2026, printed 207 of the state's 294 seats.<ref name=\"bbc\">BBC, 8 May 2026. https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwy2gp1wewjo</ref> The seat total is where those pages split.<ref name=\"hdata\" /><ref name=\"bbc\" />\n\nThe Deccan Herald, carrying PTI on 5 May 2026, says the assembly has 294 members.<ref name=\"dh\">Deccan Herald, 5 May 2026. https://www.deccanherald.com/elections/west-bengal/west-bengal-assembly-elections-2026-bjp-achieves-its-2021-target-of-crossing-200-seat-mark-five-years-later-3991797</ref> Votes were counted for 293 because one seat was countermanded.<ref name=\"dh\" /> That is the Herald's reason for the smaller number.<ref name=\"dh\" /> The papers that printed 293 were printing a count, not a smaller house.<ref name=\"dh\" /><ref name=\"hdata\" />\n\n== The rest of the board ==\nThePrint's board besides the two large parties was Congress 2, the Aam Janata Unnayan Party 2, the CPI(M) 1, and the AISF 1.<ref name=\"print\" /> The Indian Express says Trinamool was reduced to 80, down from 215 in 2021.<ref name=\"ie\" /> ThePrint says about 91 lakh names were removed from the rolls.<ref name=\"print\" />\n\nThe Indian Express entry for Falta is no counting, with a repoll ordered.<ref name=\"ie\" /> In Bhabanipur, Suvendu Adhikari defeated Mamata Banerjee by over 15,000 votes.<ref name=\"ie\" />\n\n== The oath ==\nThe BBC says Adhikari was sworn in as chief minister the Saturday after counting.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> Prime Minister Narendra Modi attended the ceremony.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The same story says the result ended 15 years of Trinamool rule.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> It calls the ministry the first BJP government in the state.<ref name=\"bbc\" />\n\nThe Indian Express is the page for Falta and for Bhabanipur.<ref name=\"ie\" /> ThePrint is the page for the smaller parties and for the names taken off the rolls.<ref name=\"print\" /> The Hindu data page is the one with the vote share.<ref name=\"hdata\" /> The BBC is the one with the oath, the prime minister at the ceremony, the end of Trinamool rule, and the first BJP government in the state.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> A check of the Election Commission results page in October 2026 returned a 404. The seat figures in this article come from the newspapers above, not from that missing page.\n\nOne seat was countermanded, so the count the papers printed was 293. The chief minister took the oath with the prime minister in the room. The Election Commission results page, checked in October, was a 404.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Elections]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
