        "user": "HansardHannah",
        "daysAgo": 4,
        "comment": "expanded from the United States Holocaust Memorial Museum, the German Historical Museum, and the Bundestag text of the Enabling Act",
        "content": "{{Infobox\n| title = Adolf Hitler\n| born = 20 April 1889\n| birthplace = Braunau am Inn\n| father = Alois Hitler, tax collector\n| putsch = 8-9 November 1923, Munich\n| result = failed\n| convicted = high treason, April 1924\n| sentence = five years\n| prison = Landsberg\n| fine = 200 gold marks\n| released = December 1924\n| chancellor = 30 January 1933\n| appointed by = Hindenburg\n| enabling act = 23 March 1933\n| vote = 444 to 94\n| died = 30 April 1945\n| place of death = underground bunker, Berlin\n}}\n\n'''Adolf Hitler''' was born on 20 April 1889 in Braunau am Inn, the son of the tax collector Alois Hitler.<ref name=\"dates\">United States Holocaust Memorial Museum, Adolf Hitler: key dates. https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/adolf-hitler-key-dates</ref> The Beer Hall Putsch in Munich, on 8 and 9 November 1923, failed.<ref name=\"putsch\">United States Holocaust Memorial Museum, Beer Hall Putsch. https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/beer-hall-putsch-munich-putsch</ref> Hindenburg appointed him chancellor on 30 January 1933.<ref name=\"bio\">United States Holocaust Memorial Museum, Adolf Hitler. https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/adolf-hitler</ref> On 30 April 1945 he committed suicide in an underground bunker in Berlin.<ref name=\"dates\" />\n\n== 20 April 1889 ==\nThe key-dates page of the United States Holocaust Memorial Museum gives the birth as 20 April 1889 and the place as Braunau am Inn, and it identifies his father as Alois Hitler, a tax collector.<ref name=\"dates\" /> The German Historical Museum's LeMO text of the judgment styles the name and the date as \"Hitler Adolf, geb. am 20. 4. 89 in Braunau.\"<ref name=\"lemo\">German Historical Museum, LeMO, the judgment in the Hitler trial. https://www.dhm.de/lemo/kapitel/weimarer-republik/innenpolitik/urteil-im-hitler-prozess</ref> The museum encyclopedia uses the order Adolf Hitler and the full year 1889. The judgment text uses the order Hitler Adolf and the short date 20. 4. 89. Both place the birth in Braunau.<ref name=\"dates\" /><ref name=\"lemo\" /> The father is on the key-dates page. The judgment excerpt used here names the accused, the birth date, and the birthplace, and does not restate the father's occupation.<ref name=\"dates\" /><ref name=\"lemo\" />\n\n== November 1923 ==\nThe Beer Hall Putsch was in Munich on 8 and 9 November 1923. It failed.<ref name=\"putsch\" /> The putsch page then records the case: convicted of high treason in April 1924, sentenced to five years at Landsberg, released in December 1924.<ref name=\"putsch\" /> The key-dates page says he was sentenced to five years and served only one.<ref name=\"dates\" /> LeMO prints the judgment. It sentences \"Hitler Adolf, geb. am 20. 4. 89 in Braunau\" to five years of fortress imprisonment for high treason, with a further six months to be served before probation on the remainder was to be considered.<ref name=\"lemo\" /> The fine printed in the LeMO text of the judgment is 200 gold marks.<ref name=\"lemo\" /> \"served only one,\" \"released December 1924,\" and \"six months before probation on the remainder was to be considered\" stay with the pages that print them.<ref name=\"dates\" /><ref name=\"putsch\" /><ref name=\"lemo\" />\n\n== 30 January 1933 ==\nHindenburg appointed him chancellor on 30 January 1933.<ref name=\"bio\" />\n\n== 23 March 1933 ==\nOn 23 March 1933 the Reichstag passed the Enabling Act by 444 votes to 94.<ref name=\"act\">German Bundestag, text of the Enabling Act. https://www.bundestag.de/resource/blob/189778/enabling_act.pdf</ref> The date, the chamber, the name of the act, and the division are what that record supplies.<ref name=\"act\" /> The appointment is the museum article. The vote is the Bundestag text.<ref name=\"bio\" /><ref name=\"act\" />\n\n== 30 April 1945 ==\nThe key-dates page states that on 30 April 1945 he committed suicide in an underground bunker in Berlin.<ref name=\"dates\" /> The place is the bunker. The city is Berlin. The act, as that page states it, is suicide.<ref name=\"dates\" />\n\n\"The Holocaust was the systematic, state-sponsored persecution and murder of six million European Jews by the Nazi German regime and its allies and collaborators.\"<ref name=\"ushmm\">United States Holocaust Memorial Museum, introduction to the Holocaust. https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/introduction-to-the-holocaust</ref>\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:History]]\n"
