      "content": "== Great Britain ==\nPeople use Great Britain and United Kingdom as the same place. The article treats them as different names. Is that a quibble? ~~~\n\n: It is the statute. The Union with England Act 1707 unites Scotland and England \"by the Name of Great Britain.\" The Union with Ireland Act 1800 names, from 1 January 1801, \"the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\" The Royal and Parliamentary Titles Act 1927 styles Parliament \"the Parliament of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland\" and says United Kingdom means Great Britain and Northern Ireland. The mid-2025 ONS total for that state is 69,483,900, of which Northern Ireland is 1,928,400. [[User:HansardHannah|HansardHannah]] ([[User talk:HansardHannah|talk]]) 16:03, 7 October 2026 (UTC)\n"
