        "content": "{{true and funny|source=Focus Features; Deadline, 1 May 2025 and 28 August 2025; Focus Features, 29 August 2025; Box Office Mojo; Hollywood Reporter, 28 August 2025}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Bugonia (film)\n| director = Yorgos Lanthimos\n| writer = Will Tracy\n| distributor = Focus Features\n| genres = thriller and dark comedy\n| limited release = 24 October 2025\n| wide release = 31 October 2025\n| world premiere = 28 August 2025, 82nd Venice Film Festival\n| premiere hall = Sala Grande\n| ovation = six minutes, Hollywood Reporter\n| runtime = two hours, Hollywood Reporter\n| domestic = $17,692,390\n| international = $25,842,102\n| worldwide = $43,534,492\n| earlier film = Save the Green Planet\n}}\n\n'''Bugonia''' is a thriller and a dark comedy directed by Yorgos Lanthimos and written by Will Tracy.<ref name=\"focus\">Focus Features, Bugonia. https://www.focusfeatures.com/bugonia</ref> Focus Features dates the release to 24 October 2025.<ref name=\"focus\" /> The cast on that page is Emma Stone, Jesse Plemons, Aidan Delbis, Stavros Halkias, and Alicia Silverstone.<ref name=\"focus\" />\n\n== The description ==\nThe studio's own description is one sentence. \"Two conspiracy obsessed young men kidnap the high-powered CEO of a major company, convinced that she is an alien intent on destroying planet Earth.\"<ref name=\"focus\" /> The kidnappers in that sentence are two. The person kidnapped is a CEO. The belief in the sentence is that she is an alien, and that the alien means to destroy the planet.<ref name=\"focus\" />\n\nFocus calls the film a thriller and a dark comedy, and it names Lanthimos as director and Tracy as writer.<ref name=\"focus\" /> The cast list on the same page runs to five names. Stone is first. Silverstone is last.<ref name=\"focus\" />\n\n== The film it remakes ==\nDeadline, on 1 May 2025, calls it a remake of the South Korean film ''Save the Green Planet''.<ref name=\"may\">Deadline, 1 May 2025. https://deadline.com/2025/05/emma-stone-bugonia-release-date-1236383271/</ref> The same story dates a limited release to 24 October and a wide release to 31 October.<ref name=\"may\" /> The studio page's release date is the October day Deadline assigns to the limited opening.<ref name=\"focus\" /><ref name=\"may\" />\n\nThe remake credit and the two October dates are Deadline's, in a story published in May. The plot sentence is the studio's, on the film's own page.<ref name=\"focus\" /><ref name=\"may\" />\n\n== Venice ==\nA Focus Features article dated 29 August 2025 says the cast and crew were at the 82nd Venice Film Festival for the world premiere the day before.<ref name=\"venice\">Focus Features, 29 August 2025. https://www.focusfeatures.com/article/bugonia-premieres-at-venice</ref> That previous day is 28 August.<ref name=\"venice\" /> The Hollywood Reporter, dated that premiere day, places the world premiere in the Sala Grande.<ref name=\"thr\">Hollywood Reporter, 28 August 2025. https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/emma-stone-bugonia-movie-venice-film-festival-1236355519/</ref>\n\nThe Reporter calls the reception a rousing six-minute standing ovation.<ref name=\"thr\" /> The runtime in that review is two hours.<ref name=\"thr\" /> The names the Reporter attaches to the premiere are Stone, Plemons, and Delbis, and the distributor it names is Focus.<ref name=\"thr\" /> Halkias and Silverstone are on the studio cast list. They are not the three names in the Reporter's premiere story.<ref name=\"focus\" /><ref name=\"thr\" />\n\nDeadline's interview story is the same premiere day. Lanthimos says: \"Not much of the dystopia in this film is very fictional. A lot of it is very reflective of the real world.\"<ref name=\"lanth\">Deadline, 28 August 2025. https://deadline.com/2025/08/yorgos-lanthimos-emma-stone-bugonia-venice-1236499764/</ref> The sentence splits the film's dystopia into a small fictional part and a large part he calls reflective of the real world.<ref name=\"lanth\" /> The ovation timing is the Reporter's. The director's line about the real world is Deadline's. Both pieces are dated 28 August 2025.<ref name=\"thr\" /><ref name=\"lanth\" />\n\n== The gross ==\nBox Office Mojo lists domestic receipts of $17,692,390.<ref name=\"mojo\">Box Office Mojo, Bugonia. https://www.boxofficemojo.com/title/tt12300742/</ref> International receipts on that page are $25,842,102.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> The worldwide total on that page is $43,534,492.<ref name=\"mojo\" /> Mojo dates the domestic release to 24 October 2025.<ref name=\"mojo\" />\n\nThe domestic figure, the international figure, and the worldwide total are three fields on one page. Deadline's wide date, 31 October, is not the date Mojo prints for the domestic release.<ref name=\"may\" /><ref name=\"mojo\" /> The studio page and Mojo agree on 24 October for the release they each describe. Deadline is the page that adds the later, wide date.<ref name=\"focus\" /><ref name=\"may\" /><ref name=\"mojo\" />\n\nThe studio's description is two men and a CEO they think is an alien. Venice stood for six minutes. The worldwide gross was $43.5 million.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Films]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
