        "content": "{{true and funny|source=IBDB; The Standard, 19 November 2024; Billboard, 8 February 2019; BBC, 4 June 2017; Playbill, 7 June 2024; Playbill, 3 June 2025}}\n{{Infobox\n| title = Ariana Grande\n| born = 26 June 1993, Boca Raton, Florida\n| broadway = Charlotte in 13, Bernard B. Jacobs Theatre\n| broadway dates = 5 October 2008 to 4 January 2009\n| also = understudy for Patrice\n| debut age in the Standard = 15\n| later television = Nickelodeon's Victorious\n| screen role = Glinda\n| elphaba = Cynthia Erivo\n| part one in the Standard = 22 November 2024, UK and US\n| part one in the 2024 Playbill = this Thanksgiving\n| for good in the 2024 Playbill = Thanksgiving 2025\n| for good in the 2025 Playbill = November 21\n| fifth album = thank u, next\n| album arrival = just after midnight, Friday 8 February 2019\n| benefit = One Love Manchester, Old Trafford\n| sellout = 50,000-capacity ground, 20 minutes\n}}\n\n'''Ariana Grande''' was born on 26 June 1993 in Boca Raton, Florida.<ref name=\"ibdb\">Internet Broadway Database, Ariana Grande. https://www.ibdb.com/broadway-cast-staff/ariana-grande-480685</ref> IBDB lists her as the original Charlotte in ''13'' at the Bernard B. Jacobs Theatre, from 5 October 2008 to 4 January 2009.<ref name=\"ibdb\" /> The same credit says she was the understudy for Patrice.<ref name=\"ibdb\" />\n\n== Fifteen ==\nThe Standard, on 19 November 2024, says the Broadway debut in ''13'' came at 15.<ref name=\"standard\">The Standard, 19 November 2024. https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/film/wicked-movie-release-date-cynthia-erivo-ariana-grande-musical-b1067375.html</ref> IBDB's dates for that run start on 5 October 2008. The birth date on IBDB is 26 June 1993.<ref name=\"ibdb\" /> The age in the Standard's sentence is 15. The theatre, the part, the understudy credit, and the closing date are IBDB's.<ref name=\"ibdb\" /><ref name=\"standard\" />\n\nThe Standard says she later appeared on Nickelodeon's ''Victorious''.<ref name=\"standard\" /> The same piece says she plays Glinda in ''Wicked: Part One''.<ref name=\"standard\" /> It dates the UK and US release of that film to 22 November 2024.<ref name=\"standard\" />\n\n== The fifth album ==\nBillboard describes ''thank u, next'' as her fifth studio album.<ref name=\"billboard\">Billboard, 8 February 2019. https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/ariana-grande-thank-u-next-stream-it-now-8497233/</ref> It dropped just after midnight on Friday 8 February 2019.<ref name=\"billboard\" /> Billboard says that was less than a year after ''Sweetener''.<ref name=\"billboard\" />\n\nThe album's number in her discography, on that story, is fifth. The clock time is just after midnight. The day Billboard names is a Friday, and the date is the story's own date.<ref name=\"billboard\" /> ''Sweetener'' is the album Billboard puts less than a year earlier. This article does not add a release date the story does not print.<ref name=\"billboard\" />\n\n== Old Trafford ==\nThe BBC, on 4 June 2017, reported One Love Manchester at Old Trafford.<ref name=\"bbc\">BBC News, 4 June 2017. https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-40134567</ref> She performed.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The ground's capacity in that report is 50,000. It sold out in 20 minutes.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> Proceeds were for people affected by the 22 May attack at the end of her Manchester Arena show.<ref name=\"bbc\" />\n\nThe capacity and the sellout time are the BBC's figures for that ground and that night. The date the BBC gives the earlier show's ending is 22 May. This article does not describe the attack.<ref name=\"bbc\" /> The fact the report adds is the purpose of the proceeds, and the fact beside it is the sellout.<ref name=\"bbc\" />\n\n== Glinda, twice ==\nPlaybill, on 7 June 2024, says the films co-star Grande as Glinda and Cynthia Erivo as Elphaba.<ref name=\"pb24\">Playbill, 7 June 2024. https://playbill.com/article/ariana-grande-dropped-hints-shed-be-glinda-on-screen-before-it-was-announced</ref> That piece says the first film is this Thanksgiving.<ref name=\"pb24\" /> It says the second part is Thanksgiving 2025.<ref name=\"pb24\" />\n\nThe Standard's date for the first film in the UK and the US is 22 November 2024.<ref name=\"standard\" /> Playbill's phrase, in the piece dated 7 June of that year, is \"this Thanksgiving.\"<ref name=\"pb24\" /> Both wordings stay. The Standard names a calendar day. That earlier Playbill names the holiday.<ref name=\"standard\" /><ref name=\"pb24\" />\n\nPlaybill, on 3 June 2025, says ''Wicked: For Good'' will arrive November 21.<ref name=\"pb25\">Playbill, 3 June 2025. https://playbill.com/article/get-a-1st-look-at-ariana-grande-cynthia-erivo-jonathan-bailey-more-in-wicked-for-good</ref> Erivo and Grande are Elphaba and Glinda, respectively.<ref name=\"pb25\" /> The first film, that piece says, earned 2025 Academy Awards for costumes and for production design.<ref name=\"pb25\" /> It was nominated for 10 categories, including Best Picture.<ref name=\"pb25\" />\n\nThe 2024 Playbill's timing for the second part is Thanksgiving 2025. The later Playbill's timing is November 21.<ref name=\"pb24\" /><ref name=\"pb25\" /> The awards sentence covers costumes and production design, and the nomination count includes Best Picture. The count Playbill prints is 10.<ref name=\"pb25\" />\n\nThe benefit concert sold out a 50,000-capacity ground in 20 minutes. She had opened on Broadway at 15, as Charlotte, and she understudied Patrice.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Musicians]]\n[[Category:True but improbable]]\n"
