        "user": "CiteOrDie",
        "daysAgo": 4,
        "comment": "expanded from the BBC, the Guardian, the court-letter report, the 2019 interview, and SOAR",
        "content": "{{Infobox\n| title = Virginia Giuffre\n| died = 25 April 2025, aged 41\n| place = her farm in Western Australia, Friday night\n| family = said she died by suicide\n| police = a 41-year-old woman found unresponsive in Neergabby; death not suspicious\n| settlement letter = 15 February 2022\n| sum = not disclosed\n| liability = no admission\n| donation = a substantial donation to her charity\n| memoir = Nobody's Girl, about 400 pages\n| co-author = Amy Wallace\n| publisher = Knopf\n| publication announced = BBC, 25 August 2025, for October 2025\n| charity = SOAR, Speak Out, Act, Reclaim\n| charity form = 501(c)(3)\n}}\n\n'''Virginia Giuffre''' died on the night of Friday 25 April 2025, aged 41, at her farm in Western Australia. Her family said she died by suicide. The BBC and the Guardian both reported the family's account on 26 April 2025.<ref name=\"bbcdeath\">BBC News, 26 April 2025. https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cql67qk0dd3o</ref><ref name=\"guarddeath\">The Guardian, 26 April 2025. https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/26/virginia-giuffre-suicide-dead-aged-41</ref> Police said a 41-year-old woman was found unresponsive in Neergabby and that the death was not suspicious.<ref name=\"bbcdeath\" /> The family said suicide. The police statement used here does not say that.<ref name=\"bbcdeath\" /><ref name=\"guarddeath\" />\n\n== What the family said, and what police said ==\nThe police sentence does not use the word suicide. The family's sentence does. They are not the same finding. Neergabby is the place in the police sentence. The farm in Western Australia is the place in the family's sentence.<ref name=\"bbcdeath\" /><ref name=\"guarddeath\" />\n\n== The letter of 15 February 2022 ==\nA court letter of 15 February 2022, reported by the BBC, said the settlement sum \"is not being disclosed.\" There was no admission of liability. There was to be a \"substantial donation\" to her charity.<ref name=\"bbccourt\">BBC News, 15 February 2022. https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-60393843</ref> The letter does not print a figure.<ref name=\"bbccourt\" /> The same day's Guardian report carried estimates from lawyers, and the estimates are not the letter. International lawyers estimated more than $10 million before Prince Andrew's legal bill. Ann Olivarius expected at least £10 million.<ref name=\"guardset\">The Guardian, 15 February 2022. https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/feb/15/prince-andrew-and-virginia-giuffre-reach-settlement-in-principle</ref> Those are estimates given to the Guardian. They are not a sum the court letter disclosed.<ref name=\"bbccourt\" /><ref name=\"guardset\" />\n\n== The interview of 17 November 2019 ==\nOn 17 November 2019, in a BBC Newsnight interview, Prince Andrew said: \"I'd taken Beatrice to a Pizza Express in Woking\" and \"going to Pizza Express in Woking is an unusual thing for me to do.\"<ref name=\"newsnight\">BBC News, 17 November 2019, the Newsnight interview. https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-50449339</ref> The Guardian's settlement article quotes him from the same interview on a medical claim: \"I have a peculiar medical condition which is that I don't sweat or I didn't sweat at the time.\" He tied that claim to \"an overdose of adrenalin in the Falkland's War.\"<ref name=\"guardset\" /> The Pizza Express sentences are the BBC's quotation. The sweating sentence, and the Falkland's War sentence he attached to it, are the Guardian settlement article's quotation.<ref name=\"newsnight\" /><ref name=\"guardset\" />\n\n== Nobody's Girl ==\nThe memoir is ''Nobody's Girl''. It is about 400 pages, written with Amy Wallace. Knopf said she wanted it published if she died. On 25 August 2025 the BBC said publication would be in October 2025.<ref name=\"book\">BBC News, 25 August 2025. https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c2djy7048pdo</ref>\n\n== SOAR ==\nShe founded SOAR, Speak Out, Act, Reclaim. It is a 501(c)(3) for survivors of sex trafficking, abuse, and domestic violence.<ref name=\"soar\">SOAR, about the organisation. https://www.speakoutactreclaim.org/about-us</ref> The \"substantial donation\" in the 2022 court letter was to her charity.<ref name=\"bbccourt\" /><ref name=\"soar\" />\n\nThe court letter said the sum was not being disclosed. The book was called Nobody's Girl.\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:People]]\n[[Category:2025 deaths]]\n"
